<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Aragats</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aragats</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Aragats is the highest mountain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, an extinct volcano rising to 4,090 metres north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yerevan">Yerevan</a>. Its slopes have been settled since prehistoric times and carry the medieval fortress of Amberd and the Byurakan Astrophysical Observatory. In the 9th and 8th centuries BCE the lands below it were part of Etiuni, which the kings of Urartu repeatedly attacked.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-aragats.jpg" alt="Mount Aragats" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Armenak Margarian · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Aragats_2020-05-11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
